.TH IO_ADDBUF_S_FREE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
iob_adds_free \- Add a string to an I/O batch buffer and free the string when done

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/iob.h>

.IB int
.IB iob_adds_free(
.IB io_batch* b,
.IB const char* s
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBiob_adds_free\fR function adds a string to an I/O batch buffer and frees the string once the data has been added. This function is useful when the string is no longer needed after being added to the batch.

The function takes the following parameters:

.IB b
Pointer to the I/O batch buffer.

.IB s
Pointer to the string to be added.

The function returns 0 on success, or a negative value indicating an error.

The function is part of the \fBiob\fR library, which provides a framework for managing I/O operations in batch mode.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBiob_adds_free\fR function to add a string to an I/O batch buffer and free the string:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/iob.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
  io_batch batch;
  char* str = strdup("Hello, World!");

  if (!str) {
    perror("strdup");
    return 1;
  }

  io_batch_init(&batch);

  if (iob_adds_free(&batch, str) != 0) {
    perror("iob_adds_free");
    free(str);
    return 1;
  }

  if (iob_execute(&batch) != 0) {
    perror("iob_execute");
    free(str);
    return 1;
  }

  printf("String added to batch buffer and string freed\n");

  return 0;
}
.nef